+++ b/docs/extensions/footnotes.md
@@ -98,6 +98,16 @@ The following options are provided to configure the output:
 * **`SEPARATOR`**:
     The text string used to set the footnote separator. Defaults to `:`.
 
+* **`USE_DEFINITION_ORDER`**:
+    Whether to order footnotes by definition order (`True`) or by reference
+    order (`False`). Defaults to `False`.
+
+    By default, footnotes are numbered and listed in the order in which they
+    are first referenced in the document. Footnotes which are defined but never
+    referenced are listed after all referenced footnotes, in definition order.
+    Set this option to `True` to number and list footnotes in the order in
+    which they are defined.
+
 A trivial example:
 
 ```python
